---
/**
 * Track 8 (Visual Math: Calculus), Lesson 6, illustration.
 *
 * The chain rule as a left-to-right pipeline. An input x flows into the
 * inner function g, producing an intermediate value u = g(x), which then
 * flows into the outer function f, producing the output f(u) = f(g(x)).
 * The first arrow (the inner stage) is labeled with its local rate g'(x);
 * the second arrow (the outer stage) is labeled with its local rate f'(u).
 * The punchline below: the overall rate of change is the PRODUCT of the
 * two stage rates, f'(g(x)) · g'(x). Nudge x a little, g amplifies it by
 * g'(x), then f amplifies that by f'(u); the amplifications multiply.
 */

// Pipeline vertical center
const cyP = 150;

// Node geometry (input chip, function box, intermediate chip, function box, output chip)
const NODE_H = 52;       // height of the small value chips
const BOX_H = 78;        // height of the function boxes (taller, the "machines")
const CHIP_W = 92;       // width of value chips (x, u, f(u))
const BOX_W = 110;       // width of function boxes (g, f)
const GAP = 26;          // horizontal gap between a node and the next

// Left edge of each element, laid out in sequence
const x0 = 36;                          // input chip x
const x1 = x0 + CHIP_W + GAP;           // inner box (g) x
const x2 = x1 + BOX_W + GAP;            // intermediate chip (u) x
const x3 = x2 + CHIP_W + GAP;           // outer box (f) x
const x4 = x3 + BOX_W + GAP;            // output chip f(u) x

const TEAL = '#0d9488';
const AMBER = '#d97706';
const ACCENT = '#7c3aed';
const SKY = '#0284c7';
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 720 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca-chain-title ca-chain-desc">
		<title id="ca-chain-title">A left-to-right pipeline composing two functions, with the chain rule below: the total rate is the product of the two stage rates</title>
		<desc id="ca-chain-desc">A horizontal pipeline of five elements. From the left: a value chip holding the input x; an arrow labeled with the inner rate g prime of x; a function box for the inner function g; the intermediate value chip holding u equals g of x; a second arrow labeled with the outer rate f prime of u; a function box for the outer function f; and a final value chip holding the output f of u, which is f of g of x. The inner stage and its rate are drawn in sky blue, the outer stage and its rate in amber. Below the pipeline, in a rounded box, the punchline reads: total rate equals f prime of g of x times g prime of x, the two stage rates multiplied. A short caption notes that a small nudge in x is amplified by g prime of x, then by f prime of u, so the amplifications multiply.</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker id="ca-chain-arrow-in" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill={SKY} />
			</marker>
			<marker id="ca-chain-arrow-out" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill={AMBER} />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		{/* heading */}
		<text x={360} y={36} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">composing two functions: f(g(x))</text>

		{/* input chip: x */}
		<g>
			<rect x={x0} y={cyP - NODE_H / 2} width={CHIP_W} height={NODE_H} rx="8" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.05" />
			<rect x={x0} y={cyP - NODE_H / 2} width={CHIP_W} height={NODE_H} rx="8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.45" />
			<text x={x0 + CHIP_W / 2} y={cyP - 6} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6">input</text>
			<text x={x0 + CHIP_W / 2} y={cyP + 15} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">x</text>
		</g>

		{/* arrow 1: x -> g, labeled with inner rate g'(x) */}
		<line x1={x0 + CHIP_W + 4} y1={cyP} x2={x1 - 6} y2={cyP} stroke={SKY} stroke-width="2.2" marker-end="url(#ca-chain-arrow-in)" />
		<text x={(x0 + CHIP_W + x1) / 2} y={cyP - 14} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={SKY}>g'(x)</text>
		<text x={(x0 + CHIP_W + x1) / 2} y={cyP + 22} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill={SKY} opacity="0.8">inner rate</text>

		{/* inner function box: g */}
		<g>
			<rect x={x1} y={cyP - BOX_H / 2} width={BOX_W} height={BOX_H} rx="10" fill={SKY} fill-opacity="0.12" stroke={SKY} stroke-width="1.6" />
			<text x={x1 + BOX_W / 2} y={cyP - 14} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill={SKY} opacity="0.85">inner function</text>
			<text x={x1 + BOX_W / 2} y={cyP + 12} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="20" font-weight="700" fill={SKY}>g</text>
			<text x={x1 + BOX_W / 2} y={cyP + 28} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="10" fill={SKY} opacity="0.8">u = g(x)</text>
		</g>

		{/* intermediate chip: u = g(x) */}
		<g>
			<rect x={x2} y={cyP - NODE_H / 2} width={CHIP_W} height={NODE_H} rx="8" fill={ACCENT} fill-opacity="0.08" />
			<rect x={x2} y={cyP - NODE_H / 2} width={CHIP_W} height={NODE_H} rx="8" fill="none" stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.8" />
			<text x={x2 + CHIP_W / 2} y={cyP - 6} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill={ACCENT} opacity="0.75">intermediate</text>
			<text x={x2 + CHIP_W / 2} y={cyP + 16} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>u = g(x)</text>
		</g>

		{/* arrow 2: u -> f, labeled with outer rate f'(u) */}
		<line x1={x2 + CHIP_W + 4} y1={cyP} x2={x3 - 6} y2={cyP} stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="2.2" marker-end="url(#ca-chain-arrow-out)" />
		<text x={(x2 + CHIP_W + x3) / 2} y={cyP - 14} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>f'(u)</text>
		<text x={(x2 + CHIP_W + x3) / 2} y={cyP + 22} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill={AMBER} opacity="0.85">outer rate</text>

		{/* outer function box: f */}
		<g>
			<rect x={x3} y={cyP - BOX_H / 2} width={BOX_W} height={BOX_H} rx="10" fill={AMBER} fill-opacity="0.12" stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="1.6" />
			<text x={x3 + BOX_W / 2} y={cyP - 14} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill={AMBER} opacity="0.9">outer function</text>
			<text x={x3 + BOX_W / 2} y={cyP + 12} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="20" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>f</text>
			<text x={x3 + BOX_W / 2} y={cyP + 28} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="10" fill={AMBER} opacity="0.85">f(u)</text>
		</g>

		{/* output chip: f(u) */}
		<g>
			<rect x={x4} y={cyP - NODE_H / 2} width={CHIP_W} height={NODE_H} rx="8" fill={TEAL} fill-opacity="0.1" />
			<rect x={x4} y={cyP - NODE_H / 2} width={CHIP_W} height={NODE_H} rx="8" fill="none" stroke={TEAL} stroke-width="1.4" opacity="0.9" />
			<text x={x4 + CHIP_W / 2} y={cyP - 6} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill={TEAL} opacity="0.85">output</text>
			<text x={x4 + CHIP_W / 2} y={cyP + 16} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={TEAL}>f(u)</text>
		</g>

		{/* punchline: total rate is the product of the two stage rates */}
		<g transform="translate(150, 248)">
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="420" height="86" rx="8" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.04" />
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="420" height="86" rx="8" fill="none" stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.5" />
			<text x="210" y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">the overall rate is the product of the stage rates:</text>
			<text x="210" y="56" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="17" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">
				(f∘g)'(x) = <tspan fill={AMBER}>f'(g(x))</tspan> · <tspan fill={SKY}>g'(x)</tspan>
			</text>
			<text x="210" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6">(outer rate at u = g(x)), times (inner rate at x)</text>
		</g>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>Read it left to right: a small nudge in x is first amplified by the inner rate g'(x), turning into a nudge in u = g(x); that nudge is then amplified by the outer rate f'(u). Two amplifications in a row multiply, so the total rate of change is f'(g(x)) times g'(x). That product is the chain rule.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 740px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
